invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the round XORs the round constant into lane 0 twice, so iota
  adds nothing and the four states run a permutation without it. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    a[0] = lanes_xor(a[0], round_constant);
--- new
    a[0] = lanes_xor(a[0], lanes_xor(round_constant, round_constant));
